# One proxy per line. Blank lines are ignored.
# Every proxy (HTTP/HTTPS/SOCKS5/SOCKS5h, with or without credentials) is routed
# through Lork's internal relay, so authenticated SOCKS5 works too.
#
# A bare host:port with no scheme is treated as HTTP. Use socks5:// / socks5h://
# for SOCKS. Examples (pick the format your provider gives you):
#
# ip:port
# ip:port:username:password
# username:password@ip:port
# http://user:pass@host:port
# socks5://user:pass@host:port
# socks5h://user:pass@host:port
#
# LOCAL   -> use the machine's own IP (no proxy)
